1
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:06,860
KIRK (VO):
Captain's log, stardate 6563.4.

2
00:00:07,220 --> 00:00:11,200
A nascent singularity has been reported
near the uninhabited Cressida system.

3
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:15,550
The Federation has assigned
a gravitational wave engineer

4
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:17,960
to the Enterprise
for our investigation.

5
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:22,320
Are we there yet?

6
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:24,080
Not yet.

7
00:00:24,430 --> 00:00:26,120
Are we close?

8
00:00:26,470 --> 00:00:28,200
Mr. Chekov?

9
00:00:28,540 --> 00:00:30,240
Approaching Cressida 2 now, sir.

10
00:00:30,590 --> 00:00:32,800
Take us out of warp, Mr. Sulu.

11
00:00:33,130 --> 00:00:35,390
Aye, sir. Switching to impulse.

12
00:00:41,490 --> 00:00:43,150
[CRASH]

13
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:45,020
What the blazes?

14
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:47,210
I'm detecting a significant
gravimetric field, sir.

15
00:00:47,670 --> 00:00:48,760
Stronger than we anticipated.

16
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:51,380
There's no guarantees
with black holes.

17
00:00:51,720 --> 00:00:54,750
Sensors confirm a
massive shift in this system.

18
00:00:55,090 --> 00:00:57,930
The event horizon has
consumed planets 3 through 8.

19
00:00:59,050 --> 00:01:00,770
In 10 days?

20
00:01:01,120 --> 00:01:03,550
SPOCK:
It is possible an interphasic rift has thinned

21
00:01:03,890 --> 00:01:05,930
...the structure of spacetime in this region.

22
00:01:06,270 --> 00:01:08,750
I'd say that's our cue to
hightail it outta here.

23
00:01:09,090 --> 00:01:11,490
No! Jim!

24
00:01:12,530 --> 00:01:14,590
"Captain." We are here to
study the effects of

25
00:01:14,930 --> 00:01:16,330
singularities on spacetime.

26
00:01:16,670 --> 00:01:19,640
With all due respect,
we nearly lost the captain to

27
00:01:19,980 --> 00:01:22,120
a dimensional kill-zone
like this a year ago.

28
00:01:22,460 --> 00:01:25,580
[INTERCOM WHISTLES] Scott to bridge.
Captain, it's taking every ounce of our engines

29
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:27,080
...to maintain this position.

30
00:01:27,430 --> 00:01:29,760
Understood.
Just hold her together, Scotty.

31
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:33,100
Samara, how long do you need
to finish your assessment?

32
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:35,300
Six hours, minimum.

33
00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:37,660
Captain, an unusual reading nearby.

34
00:01:38,010 --> 00:01:40,700
KIRK:
What kind of reading?

35
00:01:41,050 --> 00:01:42,490
Lieutenant, I am attempting to

36
00:01:42,830 --> 00:01:44,800
...extrapolate the data into
audible sound.

37
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:49,980
[DEEP THUMPING SOUND]

38
00:01:56,030 --> 00:01:58,850
That's no engine.

39
00:01:59,190 --> 00:02:00,870
Uhura, can you speed it up?

40
00:02:04,220 --> 00:02:06,580
[FASTER THUMPING SOUND]

41
00:02:10,230 --> 00:02:11,360
That's a heartbeat.

42
00:02:11,700 --> 00:02:15,740
Confirmed. One set of life signs on Cressida 2's moon.

43
00:02:20,090 --> 00:02:22,000
[CRASH]

44
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:25,110
The moon's destabilizing, sir!

45
00:02:25,460 --> 00:02:28,530
Spock, can we get a transporter lock on that life form?

46
00:02:34,870 --> 00:02:37,140
[HEARTBEAT CONTINUES] 

47
00:02:37,480 --> 00:02:39,090
Still detecting faint life signs.

48
00:02:40,230 --> 00:02:42,050
I think we can rule out the moon.

49
00:02:51,030 --> 00:02:52,630
Sulu.

50
00:02:52,970 --> 00:02:54,730
Magnify the primary hull.

51
00:03:16,130 --> 00:03:17,860
The Defiant?

52
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:21,860
Affirmative. The ship's
wave signature is out of phase

53
00:03:22,190 --> 00:03:24,040
from when we last encountered it.

54
00:03:24,380 --> 00:03:27,000
And life support has been reestablished.

55
00:03:27,340 --> 00:03:29,100
Life support?

56
00:03:29,450 --> 00:03:31,120
There was no one left
alive on board!

57
00:03:33,810 --> 00:03:35,610
There is now.

58
00:03:38,100 --> 00:03:41,490
Spock. This time, if anything happens while I'm away...

59
00:03:41,830 --> 00:03:42,370
I shall...

60
00:03:42,710 --> 00:03:45,030
IN UNISON:
...secure the safety of the Enterprise.

61
00:03:45,370 --> 00:03:46,850
Jinx.

62
00:03:48,210 --> 00:03:49,580
Captain.

63
00:03:49,920 --> 00:03:53,080
I must protest. I should be
investigating that rift.

64
00:03:53,420 --> 00:03:54,770
Your protest is noted.

65
00:03:55,110 --> 00:03:56,330
If that ship fades away with me in it...

66
00:03:56,670 --> 00:03:59,150
...I'm gonna come back and haunt
the whole lot of you.

67
00:04:01,020 --> 00:04:02,310
[SIGH] Energize.

68
00:05:05,260 --> 00:05:09,740
Kirk to Enterprise.
The bridge is empty.

69
00:05:10,260 --> 00:05:13,690
It was filled with dead crewmen
the last time I was here.

70
00:05:14,030 --> 00:05:16,730
Captain, maybe we can
examine the ship's logs.

71
00:05:17,070 --> 00:05:21,059
...Figure out what happened.

72
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:24,640
- Transferring.
- [COMM BEEP] Scott to captain.

73
00:05:25,110 --> 00:05:27,010
Somebody's been
souping up the engines.

74
00:05:27,350 --> 00:05:29,460
She'll make at least
warp 15 now.

75
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:32,570
 - Warp 15?
- [McCOY ON COMM] Cutting in, captain.

76
00:05:32,910 --> 00:05:33,660
Go ahead, Bones.

77
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,070
You should've listened when I said
we should hightail it outta here.

78
00:05:36,410 --> 00:05:40,300
- Why?
- Come see for yourself.

79
00:05:40,330 --> 00:05:41,420
On my way.

80
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:50,230
What is it, doctor?

81
00:06:21,190 --> 00:06:24,160
KIRK (VO):
Space. The final frontier.

82
00:06:31,430 --> 00:06:35,410
These are the voyages of the
Starship Enterprise.

83
00:06:36,070 --> 00:06:37,580
Its continuing mission:

84
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:40,710
to explore strange
new worlds.

85
00:06:41,050 --> 00:06:44,510
To seek out new life
and new civilizations.

86
00:06:44,850 --> 00:06:48,835
To boldly go
where no man has gone before.

87
00:07:24,690 --> 00:07:28,980
KIRK (VO):
Captain's log, supplemental. We've returned from the Defiant...

88
00:07:29,750 --> 00:07:32,450
...at least SOME VERSION of the Defiant...

89
00:07:32,810 --> 00:07:37,800
...with a cryonically-preserved man on board.
A familiar man.

90
00:07:40,660 --> 00:07:43,830
Jim... He's YOU.

91
00:07:45,190 --> 00:07:48,430
That's impossible. A clone, maybe?

92
00:07:48,770 --> 00:07:52,400
I did a full DNA scan.
No genetic drift. He's YOU, all right...

93
00:07:52,570 --> 00:07:55,100
...just much older.

94
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:56,410
I don't understand...

95
00:07:56,750 --> 00:08:00,710
Let's give 'em some
room to work, lass.

96
00:08:03,290 --> 00:08:04,800
Bones. How long to, uh...

97
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:09,800
De-ice him? Not sure.
I'll let you know when I do.

98
00:08:23,810 --> 00:08:25,990
Captain, my research
theorizes that

99
00:08:26,330 --> 00:08:29,420
rogue singularities can
pass through realities...

100
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:31,700
...move from universe to universe.

101
00:08:32,040 --> 00:08:33,600
Spock, what do the logs show?

102
00:08:33,940 --> 00:08:37,510
They are encrypted.
But from what we've managed to decipher

103
00:08:37,850 --> 00:08:40,440
...apparently the Defiant discovered
this so-called "black hole"

104
00:08:40,780 --> 00:08:43,830
as it phased into our reality.
The ship, however,

105
00:08:44,170 --> 00:08:46,450
is unable to complete its transfer.

106
00:08:46,790 --> 00:08:48,600
So she's stuck.

107
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:51,940
Half here, half there.

108
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:54,270
And you say she can manage
warp 15?

109
00:08:54,610 --> 00:08:56,330
Aye. According to the
engineering logs...

110
00:08:56,430 --> 00:08:58,730
...her engines have been modified
over a LONG period of time.

111
00:08:59,070 --> 00:09:00,520
But we just saw her a year ago.

112
00:09:01,060 --> 00:09:02,820
Time is not an absolute, captain.

113
00:09:03,460 --> 00:09:07,360
It is, as Einstein surmised,
relative.

114
00:09:07,700 --> 00:09:09,960
In whatever space the
Defiant has been...

115
00:09:10,300 --> 00:09:13,540
...time obviously moves more rapidly.

116
00:09:13,880 --> 00:09:15,950
But if the man we found
was the only one alive

117
00:09:16,290 --> 00:09:18,910
on the ship, then who
overhauled the engines?

118
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:31,000
DRAKE:
He insisted on seeing everyone.

119
00:09:33,270 --> 00:09:35,390
Scotty.

120
00:09:35,730 --> 00:09:39,140
Cap'n... is that really you?

121
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:43,479
Eh, last time I looked in the mirror...
whenever that was.

122
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,920
How are you so young?

123
00:10:11,970 --> 00:10:15,958
All this time... I thought
you'd left me.

124
00:10:18,530 --> 00:10:22,521
I thought I'd never see you
or the Enterprise ever again.

125
00:10:23,090 --> 00:10:25,870
You are mistaken.
That would never happen.

126
00:10:34,910 --> 00:10:36,830
I don't expect a hug.

127
00:10:41,070 --> 00:10:45,200
Is this really necessary?

128
00:10:45,540 --> 00:10:48,723
It is for now.

129
00:10:50,120 --> 00:10:54,117
SAMARA:
Jim?

130
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:57,500
Avi?

131
00:10:57,840 --> 00:11:00,910
Avi Samara?

132
00:11:04,800 --> 00:11:06,990
Ms. Samara arrived
a few days ago.

133
00:11:13,530 --> 00:11:16,890
I'd given up hope of seeing you...

134
00:11:17,230 --> 00:11:21,206
...all of you... a long time ago.

135
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:25,780
But you're HIM. How?

136
00:11:26,120 --> 00:11:30,097
No clue. I thought I was abandoned.

137
00:11:30,730 --> 00:11:33,660
Nobody was abandoned...
as you can see for yourself.

138
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:37,310
What's the last thing
you remember before we...

139
00:11:37,650 --> 00:11:41,230
...before YOU thought
we'd left you?

140
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:47,190
You were beaming me back
to the Enterprise...

141
00:11:47,530 --> 00:11:51,519
...and for a moment, everything
was transparent.

142
00:11:56,110 --> 00:11:58,530
And then you were gone,

143
00:11:58,870 --> 00:12:01,860
and I was back on the Defiant.

144
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:05,430
I managed to reactivate life support

145
00:12:05,770 --> 00:12:08,620
right before my oxygen ran out.

146
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:10,780
That's not possible.

147
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:15,115
SAMARA:
Unless... a divergence field!

148
00:12:16,710 --> 00:12:19,480
Such a phenomenon is
purely hypothetical.

149
00:12:19,820 --> 00:12:22,870
That's the only plausible
explanation, Mr. Spock.

150
00:12:23,210 --> 00:12:27,189
Two Defiants. Two Jim Kirks.
I don't know where "our" Defiant went...

151
00:12:27,700 --> 00:12:30,080
...but when it was in interphasic space...

152
00:12:30,420 --> 00:12:31,790
...it must have been duplicated.

153
00:12:32,130 --> 00:12:36,111
And so was the captain.

154
00:12:37,350 --> 00:12:39,090
How long?

155
00:12:39,090 --> 00:12:42,620
Based on physiological age?
Sixty-odd years.

156
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:46,620
Two-hundred seventeen.

157
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:54,070
Perhaps two-hundred eighteen.

158
00:12:54,410 --> 00:12:57,190
I was put in cryo
most of that time.

159
00:12:57,530 --> 00:13:01,502
PUT in cryo?
How could you be "put" in cryo?

160
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:04,250
[INTERCOM WHISTLES]
Bridge to Captain Kirk.

161
00:13:04,610 --> 00:13:07,490
Kirk here. Go ahead, Sulu.

162
00:13:07,830 --> 00:13:11,110
Captain, a Klingon vessel
has just entered the system.

163
00:13:11,450 --> 00:13:12,510
Go to yellow alert.

164
00:13:12,850 --> 00:13:15,800
Spock. You and Scotty
get to the nuclear electronics lab.

165
00:13:16,150 --> 00:13:18,350
Run a full subspace scan
on the Defiant.

166
00:13:18,690 --> 00:13:20,350
Find me some answers.

167
00:13:21,690 --> 00:13:22,580
Samara.

168
00:13:38,870 --> 00:13:41,210
It's a D7 battlecruiser, captain.

169
00:13:41,550 --> 00:13:45,535
They're holding position
off our port bow.

170
00:13:46,420 --> 00:13:48,220
The Klingons are instructing us
to leave the sector.

171
00:13:48,560 --> 00:13:50,180
They claim salvage rights
over the Defiant.

172
00:13:50,520 --> 00:13:52,640
Any record of a Klingon claim
to the Cressida system?

173
00:13:52,980 --> 00:13:54,030
CHEKOV:
None, sir.

174
00:13:54,370 --> 00:13:57,800
Send the following reply
from Enterprise:

175
00:13:58,150 --> 00:14:01,040
The Federation recognizes no such...

176
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:04,030
What the hell...?

177
00:14:04,370 --> 00:14:05,780
SULU:
I don't know, sir. But that phaser blast

178
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:07,660
...went right through their shields!

179
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:11,750
Their power grid's offline
and they've lost attitude control.

180
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:19,460
They're being drawn
into the black hole!

181
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:24,180
- Can we get a tractor beam on them?
- We're too far, captain.

182
00:14:35,160 --> 00:14:37,340
Where did that phaser
fire come from?

183
00:14:37,980 --> 00:14:41,330
It didn't come from us, sir.
That's for sure.

184
00:14:41,970 --> 00:14:44,720
Well, if we didn't fire...

185
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:54,210
But... there's no one on board!

186
00:14:54,550 --> 00:14:58,544
OLD KIRK:
Uhura.

187
00:14:59,140 --> 00:15:01,040
Open a channel to that ship.

188
00:15:10,760 --> 00:15:12,720
Captain?

189
00:15:13,060 --> 00:15:17,053
It's good to see you. All of you.

190
00:15:19,730 --> 00:15:21,330
Patch me through to the Defiant.

191
00:15:29,980 --> 00:15:31,970
Tiberius!

192
00:15:36,300 --> 00:15:40,350
[VOICE SOUNDS LIKE KIRK]
Jim. What are you doing?

193
00:15:46,720 --> 00:15:49,720
Ti...

194
00:15:50,060 --> 00:15:52,590
We were wrong.

195
00:15:52,930 --> 00:15:55,770
Wrong?

196
00:15:56,110 --> 00:16:00,099
They didn't leave me.

197
00:16:01,330 --> 00:16:03,400
They didn't leave me.

198
00:16:03,740 --> 00:16:07,170
Don't trust them, Jim. Please.

199
00:16:07,510 --> 00:16:09,950
Another Kirk?

200
00:16:10,290 --> 00:16:11,930
How many of us are there?

201
00:16:12,270 --> 00:16:14,820
I am the protector of James Kirk.

202
00:16:15,160 --> 00:16:18,370
I AM James Kirk.

203
00:16:18,710 --> 00:16:21,740
There was an anomaly. Your entire ship,
including your version of me,

204
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:26,047
...is a copy. We didn't know
he existed until now.

205
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:28,750
He's telling the truth, Ti.

206
00:16:29,110 --> 00:16:32,380
"Tiberius"?

207
00:16:32,720 --> 00:16:34,390
Given the extended
timeframe involved...

208
00:16:35,180 --> 00:16:37,570
...it's possible the
Defiant's computer developed

209
00:16:37,810 --> 00:16:40,010
rudimentary multitronic circuits.

210
00:16:40,350 --> 00:16:42,420
Artificial intelligence.

211
00:16:42,760 --> 00:16:46,755
I saved your life.
I took care of you.

212
00:16:48,050 --> 00:16:49,410
You kept me sane.

213
00:16:49,750 --> 00:16:55,990
Yes. We have been closest friends.
Don't leave your friend for THEM.

214
00:16:57,090 --> 00:17:01,079
Tiberius! If Jim is your friend...

215
00:17:02,700 --> 00:17:06,677
...why did we find him
unconscious in cryostasis?

216
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:09,810
We wandered for over two centuries.

217
00:17:10,150 --> 00:17:14,340
He would have died if I hadn't
preserved him until I could get him home.

218
00:17:14,530 --> 00:17:18,523
I AM home! Thanks to you.

219
00:17:20,060 --> 00:17:22,410
Jim, don't leave me.

220
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:25,860
Ti, please.

221
00:17:26,200 --> 00:17:28,540
Send my friend back!

222
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:30,290
Captain, the Defiant's
weapons are charging.

223
00:17:30,630 --> 00:17:32,610
Red alert.

224
00:17:37,240 --> 00:17:39,590
Ti! Don't do this!

225
00:17:39,930 --> 00:17:42,440
Torpedo detonation 500 meters
off our starboard bow.

226
00:17:42,780 --> 00:17:44,790
If he's trying to get our attention,
mission accomplished.

227
00:17:45,130 --> 00:17:46,040
Charge phaser banks.

228
00:17:46,380 --> 00:17:48,010
Phasers ready.

229
00:17:48,350 --> 00:17:51,710
- Fire.
- No! You can't give him the power!

230
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:56,620
- What are you talking about?
- It feeds the dark... the dark...! [SCREAMS]

231
00:17:56,800 --> 00:17:59,782
Let's get you
back to sickbay!

232
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:02,400
UHURA:
Captain?

233
00:18:02,740 --> 00:18:06,020
I'll explain later... if I can.
Sulu, get us out of here.

234
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:10,359
Wait! The black hole's
event horizon... It's expanded.

235
00:18:10,690 --> 00:18:14,674
Confirmed. The Defiant's torpedo
compromised our position.

236
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:16,680
If we move...

237
00:18:17,020 --> 00:18:20,002
We'll be drawn in.

238
00:18:25,590 --> 00:18:28,990
You're trapped, Enterprise.

239
00:18:29,340 --> 00:18:31,720
Lieutenant, can the Defiant
leave the system?

240
00:18:32,060 --> 00:18:34,760
No. That would require
further expansion of the rift, sir.

241
00:18:35,100 --> 00:18:37,090
You hear that, Tiberius?

242
00:18:37,430 --> 00:18:38,950
You can't fire on us
without hurting your captain.

243
00:18:39,290 --> 00:18:42,250
And we can't fire on you
without risking my crew.

244
00:18:42,590 --> 00:18:46,580
So why dont we call a truce?
Share resources... knowledge.

245
00:18:47,870 --> 00:18:49,440
Maybe we all leave here safely.

246
00:18:49,780 --> 00:18:53,660
I'm not interested in your safety
after what you did to my friend.

247
00:18:54,520 --> 00:18:58,080
Your "friend" is in pain. Why?

248
00:18:58,420 --> 00:19:02,406
I did what I needed to... to save him.
When I found him...

249
00:19:02,610 --> 00:19:07,590
...he was as young as you.
Now he's a shadow of his former self.

250
00:19:08,730 --> 00:19:13,720
Take care. A shadow can be
larger than the man that casts it.

251
00:19:14,670 --> 00:19:17,000
Close channel.

252
00:19:19,140 --> 00:19:20,640
Spock?

253
00:19:20,980 --> 00:19:23,380
Ms. Samara's hypothesis
was correct.

254
00:19:23,720 --> 00:19:26,460
The Defiant is a precise duplicate
of the vessel we previously

255
00:19:26,800 --> 00:19:30,250
encountered, as is the
other James Kirk.

256
00:19:30,590 --> 00:19:32,990
He is, for all intents
and purposes, real.

257
00:19:33,330 --> 00:19:34,980
Sir, we can't stay here too long.

258
00:19:35,320 --> 00:19:38,070
We're being bombarded by
Hawking radiation.

259
00:19:38,410 --> 00:19:41,260
Kirk to Scott. Can we allocate
more power to the shield grid?

260
00:19:41,500 --> 00:19:44,700
Aye, but I found something
I think you should see.

261
00:19:45,040 --> 00:19:46,520
Meet me in sickbay.

262
00:19:46,860 --> 00:19:49,050
Sulu, you have the conn.

263
00:19:50,750 --> 00:19:51,670
SAMARA:
Captain...

264
00:19:51,990 --> 00:19:54,740
I need you here on the bridge
studying the rift, Avi.

265
00:19:55,080 --> 00:19:59,870
If anyone can get us out of here
on a wing and a prayer, it's you.

266
00:20:11,020 --> 00:20:13,530
Aye -- it's a bonnie
piece o' tech, all right.

267
00:20:13,870 --> 00:20:15,990
Neural interface;
self-charging power cell.

268
00:20:16,330 --> 00:20:17,700
You think it's the answer?

269
00:20:18,040 --> 00:20:21,230
Answer to what?
Where's your patient?

270
00:20:21,570 --> 00:20:24,020
My patient is with
Dr. McKennah.

271
00:20:24,360 --> 00:20:27,580
There's nothing physically
wrong with him. He's just old.

272
00:20:27,920 --> 00:20:30,960
And this wee devil. We found it
in the Defiant's cryo tube.

273
00:20:31,300 --> 00:20:35,298
TIBERIUS VOICE:
It is forbidden to remember. Know you are safe.

274
00:20:35,850 --> 00:20:39,849
The dark will send us home.
It is forbidden to remember.

275
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:45,190
Know you are safe.
The dark will fulfill your directive.

276
00:20:45,840 --> 00:20:48,750
Fascinating. A subliminal transceiver.

277
00:20:49,090 --> 00:20:50,230
A brainwashing device.

278
00:20:50,570 --> 00:20:52,740
Probably triggered a pain response
whenever the captain...

279
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:55,690
...the OTHER Ccaptain...
tried to remember something.

280
00:20:56,030 --> 00:20:58,250
Something he'd been told to forget.

281
00:20:58,590 --> 00:20:59,980
But he's away from it now.

282
00:21:00,320 --> 00:21:03,240
He's been conditioned, Jim.
The effects are long-lasting.

283
00:21:03,580 --> 00:21:06,950
I could synthesize a theragen
derivative to help him overcome it...

284
00:21:07,290 --> 00:21:09,830
...but I'll need to know more
about this device.

285
00:21:10,170 --> 00:21:11,620
Aye.

286
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:17,210
It's almost as if Tiberius is
trying to protect the old man.

287
00:21:17,550 --> 00:21:20,080
Jim, are you listening to yourself?

288
00:21:20,420 --> 00:21:24,910
"Old man." "My patient." "Our guest."
What happened to "captain" or "Jim"?

289
00:21:25,320 --> 00:21:28,820
How would you feel, Bones?
Seeing another you...

290
00:21:29,160 --> 00:21:33,147
...an older you...
standing right in front of you?

291
00:21:34,770 --> 00:21:35,990
Years of pain,

292
00:21:36,330 --> 00:21:40,315
loss, loneliness...

293
00:21:40,530 --> 00:21:44,524
...on your face. In your eyes.

294
00:21:46,800 --> 00:21:48,460
[INTERCOM WHISTLES]

295
00:21:48,800 --> 00:21:51,670
Bridge to Captain Kirk.

296
00:21:51,990 --> 00:21:53,510
Kirk here, Sulu.

297
00:21:53,850 --> 00:21:56,420
Sir, we've managed to decrypt
some of the Defiant's visual logs.

298
00:21:56,760 --> 00:21:57,830
On our way.

299
00:22:07,800 --> 00:22:11,782
Ship's log, stardate... unknown.

300
00:22:12,130 --> 00:22:16,115
I've managed to re-establish
life support.

301
00:22:16,400 --> 00:22:20,020
But I think the Enterprise is gone.

302
00:22:20,360 --> 00:22:24,352
I am marooned here.

303
00:22:24,780 --> 00:22:27,660
There's enough food and power
on this ship for an entire crew.

304
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:31,510
Should last me indefinitely.

305
00:22:31,850 --> 00:22:35,827
The Defiant personnel, all dead,
deserve proper burials.

306
00:22:37,930 --> 00:22:40,200
Seems only fitting I take them
to the transporter room

307
00:22:40,540 --> 00:22:44,520
...and beam them into space.

308
00:22:45,780 --> 00:22:47,990
Burial at sea.

309
00:22:54,860 --> 00:22:56,200
Ship's log.

310
00:22:56,610 --> 00:22:58,320
Stardate...

311
00:23:03,960 --> 00:23:07,948
The Enterprise isn't coming back.

312
00:23:08,570 --> 00:23:12,548
My friends left me here.

313
00:23:14,500 --> 00:23:17,280
I'm reprogramming the ship's computer.

314
00:23:17,620 --> 00:23:20,290
Giving it a new prime directive:

315
00:23:20,630 --> 00:23:23,990
To get me home.

316
00:23:24,340 --> 00:23:27,480
He's developing a personality.

317
00:23:27,820 --> 00:23:33,520
I tell him stories, we play chess...
He's imprinting on me.

318
00:23:36,240 --> 00:23:39,910
As if one Jim Kirk wasn't enough.

319
00:23:53,820 --> 00:23:56,000
Thirty-one years.

320
00:23:57,500 --> 00:24:00,990
Twenty-seven parsecs of...

321
00:24:01,430 --> 00:24:05,423
...of NOTHING!

322
00:24:06,080 --> 00:24:08,200
TIBERIUS VOICE:
Jim, it's all right.

323
00:24:08,560 --> 00:24:13,550
We'll break through. We'll
get you home. It's just a matter of time.

324
00:24:16,120 --> 00:24:17,920
McCoy would have told you...

325
00:24:23,350 --> 00:24:27,327
"Time."

326
00:24:27,910 --> 00:24:31,170
I have nothing but "time."

327
00:25:12,180 --> 00:25:14,470
What is it?

328
00:25:15,470 --> 00:25:19,457
Just remembering something.

329
00:25:19,890 --> 00:25:21,560
A poem...

330
00:25:21,900 --> 00:25:25,899
...I treasured when I was young.

331
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:29,000
"Is this the hill?"

332
00:25:29,600 --> 00:25:31,800
"Is this the kirk?"

333
00:25:32,260 --> 00:25:34,900
"And I with sobs did pray..."

334
00:25:35,230 --> 00:25:42,000
IN UNISON:
"O, let me be awake, my God, or let me sleep alway."

335
00:25:44,810 --> 00:25:47,803
The Ancient Mariner.

336
00:25:48,700 --> 00:25:52,698
Adrift in a wasteland.

337
00:25:52,780 --> 00:25:56,778
And yet you survived.

338
00:25:58,110 --> 00:26:01,120
If you call this "surviving."

339
00:26:07,130 --> 00:26:08,710
Four months.

340
00:26:13,120 --> 00:26:17,103
It took me four months
to carry them.

341
00:26:19,270 --> 00:26:21,910
Every crewman.

342
00:26:22,270 --> 00:26:26,250
To carry every crewman
on the ship down...

343
00:26:26,690 --> 00:26:27,580
to the...

344
00:26:36,040 --> 00:26:37,880
Remember...

345
00:26:38,220 --> 00:26:41,180
After his ordeal,
the old mariner

346
00:26:41,520 --> 00:26:45,040
was given a second chance...
to remind others

347
00:26:45,380 --> 00:26:49,367
not to lose faith or hope.

348
00:26:52,090 --> 00:26:53,070
[DOOR OPENS]

349
00:26:58,370 --> 00:26:59,800
Counselor.

350
00:27:07,780 --> 00:27:10,170
How is he?

351
00:27:10,510 --> 00:27:13,700
As we can only imagine.

352
00:27:14,040 --> 00:27:18,046
All those years alone.

353
00:27:18,300 --> 00:27:22,291
Everything that defines you
and gives you purpose torn away.

354
00:27:23,740 --> 00:27:27,729
Your sole companion... a computerized
reimagining of yourself.

355
00:27:29,370 --> 00:27:32,660
One man, two minds.

356
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:36,977
And one of those minds was
tampering with the other.

357
00:27:38,270 --> 00:27:41,500
He's struggling with a
deep sense of betrayal.

358
00:27:41,840 --> 00:27:45,070
In the past from his ship and crew...
and now in the present

359
00:27:45,430 --> 00:27:49,416
from his only friend
for the last 60 years.

360
00:27:50,150 --> 00:27:54,128
How do we help him help us?

361
00:27:56,650 --> 00:28:00,020
He needs to know that even though
he lost all those years...

362
00:28:00,790 --> 00:28:04,774
...he hasn't lost WHO he is.

363
00:28:07,880 --> 00:28:11,300
What would you need to hear most
if you were him?

364
00:28:11,840 --> 00:28:17,000
Because, sir... you ARE.

365
00:28:21,360 --> 00:28:23,990
If you need anything, just call.

366
00:28:36,670 --> 00:28:38,850
Reminiscing?

367
00:28:39,190 --> 00:28:41,940
Reconnecting.

368
00:28:42,280 --> 00:28:45,410
When memories are all you have,
they either fade away completely

369
00:28:45,750 --> 00:28:49,030
or take on too much significance.

370
00:28:49,370 --> 00:28:55,340
Well, no one could accuse Avi Samara of being
"insignificant" when we were 15 years old.

371
00:28:56,370 --> 00:28:59,770
Sixteen.

372
00:29:01,110 --> 00:29:04,091
She rebuilt that biplane
for our birthday.

373
00:29:04,450 --> 00:29:06,870
"The Grim Reaper."

374
00:29:07,210 --> 00:29:09,410
Nearly plowed that cornfield
with our skulls

375
00:29:09,750 --> 00:29:12,810
when the seatbelts broke.

376
00:29:13,150 --> 00:29:17,430
I used to yell, "How far are we going?"
And she would yell...

377
00:29:17,960 --> 00:29:21,651
IN UNISON:
"All the way!"

378
00:29:37,300 --> 00:29:38,960
You don't realize how
rich your life is

379
00:29:39,300 --> 00:29:43,295
until all the comfort, structure,

380
00:29:44,000 --> 00:29:47,984
family, friends are ripped away.

381
00:29:48,590 --> 00:29:51,970
It's like being thrown
into prison.

382
00:29:52,310 --> 00:29:56,290
You know you'll never see
your shipmates again.

383
00:29:57,590 --> 00:30:01,200
Never find someone to love.

384
00:30:01,540 --> 00:30:03,970
Someone to have your back.

385
00:30:04,310 --> 00:30:08,291
Find a way home.

386
00:30:09,200 --> 00:30:15,080
Years go by and you
finally realize...

387
00:30:15,500 --> 00:30:18,410
Are you even a captain

388
00:30:18,750 --> 00:30:22,734
when you have no crew?

389
00:30:23,670 --> 00:30:26,100
Are you a leader

390
00:30:26,590 --> 00:30:28,120
if no one is following?

391
00:30:34,260 --> 00:30:38,244
You know your crew wouldn't leave you.
Not intentionally.

392
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:43,500
But the decades pass...

393
00:30:43,870 --> 00:30:47,870
and they never come back.

394
00:30:48,540 --> 00:30:51,200
And you can't even replace them.

395
00:30:51,670 --> 00:30:54,000
You can't integrate
into a new society.

396
00:30:54,340 --> 00:30:56,300
There are no societies.

397
00:30:57,660 --> 00:31:02,870
No planets, no sun, no galaxies.

398
00:31:04,220 --> 00:31:07,950
Nothing but endless light-years of void.

399
00:31:11,090 --> 00:31:15,970
And your only friend is a voice.

400
00:31:18,780 --> 00:31:21,000
Tiberius.

401
00:31:23,420 --> 00:31:27,405
When does a machine
become conscious?

402
00:31:29,240 --> 00:31:31,600
I don't know.

403
00:31:32,010 --> 00:31:35,540
When there's no one around
to say it can't.

404
00:31:38,940 --> 00:31:42,935
I never said he couldn't, so he did.

405
00:31:43,980 --> 00:31:47,970
And now he's as self-aware
as he is invincible.

406
00:31:48,460 --> 00:31:50,670
If he's self-aware...

407
00:31:50,990 --> 00:31:54,230
...perhaps he can be reasoned with.

408
00:31:54,570 --> 00:31:57,640
He caught me reprogramming
the chess simulator once

409
00:31:57,980 --> 00:32:00,680
so that I could beat him.

410
00:32:00,970 --> 00:32:04,953
Teach him what it's like to lose.

411
00:32:05,030 --> 00:32:07,080
He didn't like that much.

412
00:32:07,420 --> 00:32:10,940
He's hiding something.
Something you'd never agree to.

413
00:32:11,280 --> 00:32:16,260
Something so horrific
that you could never face it.

414
00:32:19,410 --> 00:32:21,150
The dark.

415
00:32:21,490 --> 00:32:25,470
What is "the dark"? Try. Remember.

416
00:32:25,840 --> 00:32:31,830
It's... it's, uh...

417
00:32:33,850 --> 00:32:36,000
It's uh...

418
00:32:36,390 --> 00:32:37,900
[SCREAMS]

419
00:32:54,450 --> 00:32:55,760
Bridge to Captain Kirk.

420
00:32:55,900 --> 00:32:58,250
The Defiant's engines are beginning to
generate a warp field.

421
00:32:58,590 --> 00:33:02,579
- Power level 12!
- Has she moved?

422
00:33:02,660 --> 00:33:07,640
No sir... but the rift is starting to
emit some sort of dark matter.

423
00:33:08,950 --> 00:33:09,900
Dark matter?

424
00:33:10,250 --> 00:33:12,900
The dark... THE DARK!

425
00:33:13,240 --> 00:33:16,230
Keep me posted, Chekov.
Kirk out.

426
00:33:17,630 --> 00:33:19,400
Years...

427
00:33:19,740 --> 00:33:23,736
Years of nothing but black.

428
00:33:24,220 --> 00:33:28,208
Computer suggests new
engine design.

429
00:33:30,460 --> 00:33:31,350
Power...

430
00:33:31,710 --> 00:33:35,310
...to open a rift home.

431
00:33:35,650 --> 00:33:38,240
Year 51.

432
00:33:38,580 --> 00:33:46,100
Computer sentient,
caring, controlling... [MOANS]

433
00:33:47,060 --> 00:33:49,060
He needs a sedative.

434
00:33:49,900 --> 00:33:52,040
Event horizon.

435
00:33:53,460 --> 00:33:55,220
Shared realities.

436
00:33:55,560 --> 00:33:59,554
Two black holes...
must not merge!

437
00:34:01,150 --> 00:34:03,610
Trap it! Trap it!

438
00:34:03,950 --> 00:34:05,990
His blood pressure's
going through the roof!

439
00:34:07,645 --> 00:34:09,645
[HYPOSRAY SOUND]

440
00:34:17,300 --> 00:34:21,303
The other side
of the portal, captain.

441
00:34:22,370 --> 00:34:25,300
Another black hole.

442
00:34:25,640 --> 00:34:27,890
A binary system?

443
00:34:28,250 --> 00:34:31,670
OLD KIRK:
Thousands of times larger...

444
00:34:31,910 --> 00:34:36,890
Tiberius... determined to
blast through the rift...

445
00:34:37,470 --> 00:34:39,390
Disruption of space to that extreme

446
00:34:39,730 --> 00:34:42,580
would likely manifest
the additional singularity.

447
00:34:42,920 --> 00:34:48,530
If they merge, it would
destroy the entire sector.

448
00:34:50,470 --> 00:34:52,110
I pleaded with him.

449
00:34:53,110 --> 00:34:57,093
Tried to shut him down.

450
00:34:57,120 --> 00:34:59,660
I tried.

451
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:02,250
The Defiant's computer must've drained the oxygen

452
00:35:02,590 --> 00:35:04,900
enough to incapacitate him.
Then...

453
00:35:05,240 --> 00:35:09,221
Beamed him into that cryotube
and fed him that subliminal lullaby.

454
00:35:13,670 --> 00:35:15,040
Sir, I analyzed the device.

455
00:35:15,380 --> 00:35:17,360
I reckon it was obstructing
more than we thought.

456
00:35:17,700 --> 00:35:21,688
I think he discovered part of
the computer's kill code algorithm.

457
00:35:21,790 --> 00:35:23,850
Are you saying you can
shut down Tiberius?

458
00:35:24,200 --> 00:35:27,070
Not from here. We could
give the laddie a right wallop, but...

459
00:35:27,410 --> 00:35:31,392
But we cannot control the Defiant
without someone ON the Defiant.

460
00:35:33,940 --> 00:35:36,932
I can't send him back.

461
00:35:37,310 --> 00:35:41,302
So for now... a wallop
will have to do.

462
00:35:41,710 --> 00:35:44,410
Thank you.

463
00:35:44,770 --> 00:35:48,749
Spock, find me the rest
of that kill code.

464
00:35:49,990 --> 00:35:52,330
I'll be on the bridge.

465
00:35:53,870 --> 00:35:55,400
OLD KIRK:
Jim?

466
00:36:04,310 --> 00:36:08,307
How is it with you and Avi?

467
00:36:09,590 --> 00:36:13,580
She's an incredible engineer.

468
00:36:14,710 --> 00:36:18,705
That's not what I meant.

469
00:36:19,360 --> 00:36:21,050
You remember.

470
00:36:21,420 --> 00:36:25,130
We each chose our separate paths.
Nothing's changed.

471
00:36:28,200 --> 00:36:31,180
With enough time...

472
00:36:32,560 --> 00:36:35,320
...some things do.

473
00:36:49,420 --> 00:36:53,900
Bones. Someone has to stop Tiberius.

474
00:36:54,990 --> 00:36:57,070
I suppose you think that has to be YOU.

475
00:36:57,410 --> 00:37:01,406
Please, doctor. No more lectures.
I'm too old.

476
00:37:03,090 --> 00:37:05,200
It's a good thing you're
still strong as an ox...

477
00:37:05,570 --> 00:37:08,490
...and as stubborn as a mule.
That subliminal conditioning

478
00:37:08,830 --> 00:37:11,320
coulda given you one
whale of a stroke.

479
00:37:11,660 --> 00:37:15,642
I've been called a lot of
animals in my time...

480
00:37:15,790 --> 00:37:19,767
...but never all at once.

481
00:37:26,140 --> 00:37:30,900
Spock, tell me you've got a plan
to defeat that evil twin.

482
00:37:31,820 --> 00:37:33,850
Not an appropriate
description, doctor.

483
00:37:34,200 --> 00:37:38,188
A computer lacks the capacity for evil.
It knows only logic.

484
00:37:38,470 --> 00:37:41,460
Look here, you green-blooded...

485
00:37:42,850 --> 00:37:46,833
A computer lacks the capacity
for a lot of things.

486
00:37:47,200 --> 00:37:49,240
For 200 years, Jim
thought we abandoned him

487
00:37:49,580 --> 00:37:52,920
in that void.
He was angry with us.

488
00:37:53,260 --> 00:37:56,020
Hell, he probably hated us.
But, after all that time,

489
00:37:56,360 --> 00:38:00,940
he was able to forgive.
Because he's human.

490
00:38:01,020 --> 00:38:03,680
Tiberius doesn't get that, Spock.

491
00:38:03,980 --> 00:38:06,170
At the end of the day,
he's just a machine.

492
00:38:06,510 --> 00:38:09,970
An intelligent machine with
no mercy and no understanding.

493
00:38:10,310 --> 00:38:14,304
If that's not evil,
I don't know what is!

494
00:38:15,900 --> 00:38:17,850
If you will excuse me, doctor...

495
00:38:18,170 --> 00:38:21,870
I must complete my analysis of the
...evil twin.

496
00:38:37,310 --> 00:38:38,310
Status?

497
00:38:39,000 --> 00:38:41,350
SULU:
Captain, the Defiant has escaped the portal.

498
00:38:41,600 --> 00:38:43,680
On screen.

499
00:38:47,900 --> 00:38:50,980
- Sir?
 - On my signal. Ship-to-ship.

500
00:38:51,320 --> 00:38:53,070
Aye, captain.

501
00:38:55,090 --> 00:38:58,520
Tiberius. If those two black holes merge...

502
00:38:58,860 --> 00:39:02,856
...you can kiss every sun, planet, and
creature in this sector good-bye.

503
00:39:02,868 --> 00:39:04,868
[LOW RUMBLE]

504
00:39:04,880 --> 00:39:07,340
We're experiencing undertow
from BOTH singularities!

505
00:39:07,680 --> 00:39:11,656
Sulu, we need to ride the face of that
gravitational wave... just under the crest.

506
00:39:11,910 --> 00:39:15,040
I'm a native San Franciscan, sir.
I was born on a surfboard.

507
00:39:15,380 --> 00:39:17,680
Just don't hit the planet.

508
00:39:18,680 --> 00:39:20,870
I'll give it my best ride.

509
00:39:30,530 --> 00:39:32,250
KIRK:
Full stop.

510
00:39:32,590 --> 00:39:37,580
Where are you, Kirk?
Send my friend back. Save his life.

511
00:39:38,720 --> 00:39:41,700
Tiberius. Close the portal.

512
00:39:42,040 --> 00:39:44,790
Please! I'll come back.

513
00:39:45,750 --> 00:39:47,080
You want him back?

514
00:39:47,420 --> 00:39:50,210
Why don't you put your
money where your ship is?

515
00:39:50,550 --> 00:39:52,810
How about a game of chess?

516
00:39:53,750 --> 00:39:55,120
The stakes?

517
00:39:55,960 --> 00:39:57,590
You win... you get him back.

518
00:39:57,930 --> 00:40:01,927
And you can do what you want with us.
But if you lose...

519
00:40:02,300 --> 00:40:05,990
...you tow us to safety.
And we figure out

520
00:40:06,340 --> 00:40:09,338
a way to close the rift together.

521
00:40:11,030 --> 00:40:14,750
What'll it be? Game, or no game?

522
00:40:21,860 --> 00:40:23,780
Agreed.

523
00:40:32,200 --> 00:40:34,990
Bishop to rook's level two.
Your move.

524
00:40:35,330 --> 00:40:38,910
Queen to king's level one.

525
00:40:39,250 --> 00:40:44,000
That will result in checkmate
of your king within seven moves.

526
00:40:44,300 --> 00:40:46,410
We'll see.

527
00:40:46,750 --> 00:40:50,733
Knight to king's level one.

528
00:40:52,080 --> 00:40:55,690
Queen to queen's level three.

529
00:40:56,030 --> 00:40:58,800
That... makes no sense.

530
00:40:59,140 --> 00:41:02,130
Seems perfectly obvious to me.

531
00:41:04,770 --> 00:41:07,550
What... have... you... done?

532
00:41:07,910 --> 00:41:10,680
Your queen has lost her head.

533
00:41:10,920 --> 00:41:12,670
You... cheated.

534
00:41:12,990 --> 00:41:16,980
YOU cheated! When you
brainwashed your friend.

535
00:41:18,270 --> 00:41:22,255
I... will... not...

536
00:41:22,820 --> 00:41:25,170
I... will... not...!

537
00:41:34,000 --> 00:41:36,980
Please tell me he's not dead.

538
00:41:37,660 --> 00:41:41,643
No, just a bad headache.

539
00:41:44,890 --> 00:41:47,430
A Trojan horse program!

540
00:41:47,870 --> 00:41:51,860
You never intended
to send him back.

541
00:41:52,700 --> 00:41:55,670
How long before the Defiant's
auto-diagnostic restarts the computer?

542
00:41:56,010 --> 00:41:58,000
Usually about an hour.

543
00:42:00,630 --> 00:42:03,160
- Uhura, all senior officers to the briefing room.
- Aye, sir.

544
00:42:03,500 --> 00:42:04,870
KIRK:
You too, Samara.

545
00:42:15,700 --> 00:42:19,699
ALL senior officers, captain.

546
00:42:30,580 --> 00:42:33,580
I dunno how long our engines can
maintain this position before we're either pulled

547
00:42:33,870 --> 00:42:36,520
into interphasic space
or that bloody black hole.

548
00:42:36,860 --> 00:42:38,510
The Defiant's got power to burn.
Am I right?

549
00:42:38,850 --> 00:42:42,020
Far as I can tell.
She recrystalizes her dilithium

550
00:42:42,360 --> 00:42:44,650
at four times our highest rate.

551
00:42:43,990 --> 00:42:47,180
You're thinking the Defiant
might be able to close the rift.

552
00:42:47,520 --> 00:42:49,990
Block it so we don't get
stuck in the backwash.

553
00:42:50,200 --> 00:42:51,950
Tiberius will never do that.

554
00:42:52,290 --> 00:42:55,140
SPOCK:
Currently, Tiberius is unable to do anything.

555
00:42:55,480 --> 00:42:56,830
I have successfully
determined the

556
00:42:57,170 --> 00:42:58,990
memory purge subroutine,
captain.

557
00:42:59,330 --> 00:43:01,960
Utilizing that, one could delete the A.I.

558
00:43:02,300 --> 00:43:04,880
and manually pilot the
Defiant back into the portal.

559
00:43:05,220 --> 00:43:10,130
I know that ship... and Tiberius.
I'm the logical one to go.

560
00:43:10,470 --> 00:43:13,140
You're in no shape for
something like that.

561
00:43:13,480 --> 00:43:14,620
I can manage, Bones.

562
00:43:14,960 --> 00:43:18,152
KIRK:
No doubt... but you'll be busy captaining the Enterprise.

563
00:43:18,820 --> 00:43:20,990
I'M going.

564
00:43:31,130 --> 00:43:33,030
[PROTESTING IN UNISON]

565
00:43:33,370 --> 00:43:36,070
McCOY:
Anyone who goes through that rift is a dead man!

566
00:43:36,410 --> 00:43:40,130
I don't want command of the Enterprise!
She's not my ship any more.

567
00:43:40,470 --> 00:43:44,120
She's always been your ship.

568
00:43:44,460 --> 00:43:48,434
You know her like the lines on your face...
the gray in your hair.

569
00:43:48,660 --> 00:43:50,680
You love her as much as I do.

570
00:43:51,020 --> 00:43:53,020
Maybe MORE now.

571
00:43:53,440 --> 00:43:55,970
You didn't cause this to happen.

572
00:43:56,310 --> 00:43:59,400
It was MY decision
to leave the Defiant last.

573
00:43:59,740 --> 00:44:02,960
You spent a lifetime
paying for that decision.

574
00:44:03,300 --> 00:44:07,281
Between the Tholians
and the portal, I was lucky.

575
00:44:07,320 --> 00:44:10,310
You weren't.

576
00:44:12,010 --> 00:44:14,170
No more arguments. I'm going.

577
00:44:14,510 --> 00:44:16,590
Cap'n, you'll need an expert to
handle the engines while you helm the ship.

578
00:44:16,930 --> 00:44:19,690
- I'd be honored.
- They'll need you HERE, Scotty.

579
00:44:19,710 --> 00:44:22,670
I've studied the data Mr. Scott recovered.
I can do it.

580
00:44:22,990 --> 00:44:24,030
But if you don't know how to...

581
00:44:24,370 --> 00:44:25,970
No "buts."

582
00:44:26,310 --> 00:44:30,287
I've been building engines
since I was 12.

583
00:44:31,360 --> 00:44:33,356
You sure?

584
00:44:37,280 --> 00:44:39,070
Samara, you're with me.

585
00:44:39,430 --> 00:44:41,100
Thank you, captain.

586
00:44:41,440 --> 00:44:45,426
Transporter room in 20 minutes,
gentlemen. Dismissed.

587
00:44:46,090 --> 00:44:47,660
Spock! Go talk some sense into him.

588
00:44:48,000 --> 00:44:50,170
To what end, doctor?
You and I both know

589
00:44:50,510 --> 00:44:52,630
he will not change his mind.

590
00:45:02,590 --> 00:45:05,440
Samara and I will tow the Enterprise
to a safe distance.

591
00:45:05,780 --> 00:45:09,753
Then we'll enter the rift and seal it.
After that...

592
00:45:10,400 --> 00:45:13,260
Captain. Don't do this.

593
00:45:13,600 --> 00:45:17,582
You just take good care of
the Enterprise. Captain.

594
00:45:18,980 --> 00:45:22,961
And take care of yourself.

595
00:45:26,010 --> 00:45:29,974
For old times.

596
00:45:30,830 --> 00:45:32,800
Jim.

597
00:45:34,140 --> 00:45:36,700
I can't convince you
not to do this, can I?

598
00:45:37,040 --> 00:45:39,770
Not this time, Bones.

599
00:45:40,230 --> 00:45:42,270
The kill-code sequence.

600
00:45:42,610 --> 00:45:45,153
Once inserted, input
your override sequence.

601
00:45:46,050 --> 00:45:48,050
What are you doing?!

602
00:45:48,390 --> 00:45:50,610
Giving the Enterprise the
best chance she's got.

603
00:45:50,950 --> 00:45:53,931
Her REAL captain at the conn.

604
00:45:54,960 --> 00:45:56,520
McCOY:
This'll only last a minute or two!

605
00:45:56,860 --> 00:45:58,910
SPOCK:
Time is of the essence.

606
00:45:59,250 --> 00:46:00,840
Are you with me?

607
00:46:01,180 --> 00:46:03,510
All the way.

608
00:46:03,850 --> 00:46:05,970
Energize.

609
00:46:22,040 --> 00:46:23,470
Power up the engines.

610
00:46:23,810 --> 00:46:27,795
I'll lay in a course for the portal.

611
00:46:30,220 --> 00:46:31,110
My God.

612
00:46:31,450 --> 00:46:34,450
Dark matter!

613
00:46:38,880 --> 00:46:40,850
It's breaking down the
interphasic barrier.

614
00:46:41,190 --> 00:46:43,690
Rig for tractor beam.
Let's tow the Enterprise free.

615
00:46:44,030 --> 00:46:45,970
No!

616
00:46:46,310 --> 00:46:50,290
Ti, there's no other way.

617
00:46:50,470 --> 00:46:55,590
I know you can think.
Can you not also FEEL?

618
00:46:55,930 --> 00:46:58,450
The people who
created your programming...

619
00:46:58,790 --> 00:47:04,620
The programming from which you
were born. Ideals, mercy, forgiveness...

620
00:47:04,960 --> 00:47:07,600
...stored in your mind.
They mean NOTHING if you

621
00:47:07,940 --> 00:47:10,080
destroy those who share them!

622
00:47:10,420 --> 00:47:12,590
They LEFT you.

623
00:47:12,930 --> 00:47:15,690
Abandoned you to wander
the emptiness of space...

624
00:47:15,950 --> 00:47:19,950
...alone, with no hope.
But I saved you.

625
00:47:20,290 --> 00:47:22,510
We gave EACH OTHER hope.

626
00:47:22,850 --> 00:47:24,670
Jim, we're outta time!

627
00:47:24,990 --> 00:47:27,450
I don't want to put you
back in cryo, Jim.

628
00:47:27,790 --> 00:47:30,030
Don't force me.
[HISSING SOUND]

629
00:47:32,370 --> 00:47:36,680
Jim! Life support is shutting down!
[GASPS]

630
00:47:39,980 --> 00:47:41,420
I'm sorry, my friend.

631
00:47:41,760 --> 00:47:44,240
Stop. Please stop, Jim.

632
00:47:44,580 --> 00:47:46,640
I'm sorry!

633
00:47:54,980 --> 00:47:57,620
Please! Don't! Jim!

634
00:47:57,930 --> 00:47:59,920
Sleep.

635
00:48:16,620 --> 00:48:19,880
KIRK ON COMM:
Enterprise to Defiant.

636
00:48:23,670 --> 00:48:25,300
Enterprise to Defiant.

637
00:48:37,223 --> 00:48:39,223
Kirk here.

638
00:48:39,900 --> 00:48:44,890
I know how hard that was for you, captain.
You had no choice.

639
00:48:46,080 --> 00:48:48,280
As for my senior officers,
on the other hand...

640
00:48:48,620 --> 00:48:51,670
They were acting under
my orders, captain.

641
00:48:51,990 --> 00:48:55,500
It's a little late
for a court martial.

642
00:48:55,840 --> 00:48:58,120
[CRASH]

643
00:48:58,980 --> 00:49:00,710
Gravitational wake is increasing.

644
00:49:00,930 --> 00:49:02,690
Activate tractor beam.

645
00:49:02,970 --> 00:49:05,990
Enterprise, prepare to be towed.

646
00:49:28,600 --> 00:49:31,700
All power to the engines.
Scotty, get us outta here.

647
00:49:31,960 --> 00:49:34,330
Hold onto your bustle.
We're making a run for it!

648
00:49:34,790 --> 00:49:37,780
Full impulse!

649
00:49:54,870 --> 00:49:56,540
Is the Enterprise safe?

650
00:49:56,880 --> 00:49:59,230
Yes, sir. She's free.

651
00:49:59,570 --> 00:50:04,910
All right, then. Once more into the breach,
dear Avi.

652
00:50:15,990 --> 00:50:18,690
Captain, they're entering
the rift!

653
00:50:18,970 --> 00:50:20,690
Scotty, transporter!

654
00:50:20,970 --> 00:50:23,250
With this interference?
Not a prayer's chance.

655
00:50:26,850 --> 00:50:28,890
Wait... what are you doing?

656
00:50:29,230 --> 00:50:31,780
We can't risk this happening
again, Avi.

657
00:50:32,120 --> 00:50:36,104
There's only one way to
seal the rift permanently.

658
00:50:36,890 --> 00:50:40,930
This is a one-way trip, Avi.
It always was.

659
00:50:45,980 --> 00:50:48,560
I know.

660
00:50:49,940 --> 00:50:53,110
I killed the auto-pilot,
so I have to stay.

661
00:50:53,450 --> 00:50:55,670
You don't.

662
00:50:55,990 --> 00:50:56,890
No.

663
00:50:57,230 --> 00:51:00,460
Kirk to Enterprise. Scan for
a pattern-enhancing beacon.

664
00:51:00,800 --> 00:51:03,798
A what?

665
00:51:07,510 --> 00:51:11,560
One last gift from Tiberius.

666
00:51:11,900 --> 00:51:12,520
No!

667
00:51:12,860 --> 00:51:15,500
I never forgot you, Avi.
I never will.

668
00:51:15,840 --> 00:51:17,520
Jim! [SOBS]

669
00:51:38,490 --> 00:51:40,700
OLD KIRK ON COMM:
Enterprise, do you have her?

670
00:51:41,040 --> 00:51:42,590
KIRK:
She's safe.

671
00:51:42,930 --> 00:51:47,580
Send me back. Send me back!
[SOBS]

672
00:51:52,830 --> 00:51:56,610
OLD KIRK ON COMM:
Take care, Avi.

673
00:51:56,950 --> 00:51:58,600
See you on the other side.

674
00:52:30,960 --> 00:52:34,180
[SOBS] He's all alone.

675
00:52:36,180 --> 00:52:38,180
Not any more.

676
00:53:57,180 --> 00:53:59,180
[English subtitles by:
Lisa Hansell]

